1
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:20,603
So even if Columbus got lost and
wasn't the first to discover America,

2
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,397
he's still my hero.

3
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:26,568
He was really brave to sail such
a tiny ship over a really big ocean,

4
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:29,154
and because of him, we get
Columbus Day off of school.

5
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:36,786
Thank you, Heather.
Ronnie, tell us about your hero.

6
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:52,427
What's he writing?

7
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:56,306
Hachiko was my grandfather
Wilson's dog.

8
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:01,895
Everyone called Hachi
a mystery dog

9
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:05,398
because they never really knew
where he came from.

10
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:09,819
Maybe Hachi escaped from a dog pound.

11
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:12,906
Or maybe he jumped out
of somebody's car

12
00:01:12,947 --> 00:01:16,451
from someplace far away like
Florida or New Jersey.

13
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:22,749
But no matter how,
Hachi was lost.

14
00:02:29,649 --> 00:02:31,735
Hey, it's a little puppy.

15
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:53,798
But no matter how it happened,

16
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:58,595
a long time ago, in the town
my grandfather lived in,

17
00:02:58,636 --> 00:03:01,765
Hachi appeared
at the train station,

18
00:03:01,806 --> 00:03:04,309
and that's where
their story began.

19
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:46,851
No, it was great.
I loved the musicians.

20
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:49,145
No, no, no,
I'll walk. I'll walk.

21
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:52,565
Yeah, I love you, too. Bye.

22
00:03:55,944 --> 00:03:59,823
Hey, buddy. Are you lost?
Come here.

23
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:07,539
You lost here, bud?

24
00:04:09,207 --> 00:04:11,209
Someone must be
looking for you.

25
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:18,216
Little guy was
wandering around.

26
00:04:18,299 --> 00:04:19,426
Really? Out on the platform?

27
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:21,094
On the platform, yeah.

28
00:04:21,177 --> 00:04:22,679
Well, good for you
for finding him.

29
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:24,097
Yeah.

30
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:26,307
Well, I'll tell you what.

31
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:28,226
This little crate was
out there. It was broken.

32
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:29,853
I don't know
what's going on, but...

33
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:33,273
Anyhow, someone's gonna
be here for him. Yeah.

34
00:04:33,356 --> 00:04:35,442
So if you'll just
hold him here.

35
00:04:35,483 --> 00:04:36,526
You just hold him
till they come.

36
00:04:36,609 --> 00:04:38,528
No, I can't do that.

37
00:04:38,611 --> 00:04:40,196
I can't do that,
Professor.

38
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:43,116
Well, he was out... No one's
gonna leave this dog. There's...

39
00:04:43,158 --> 00:04:45,660
No, I know that.
I know no one's gonna leave it.

40
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:48,663
They'll be back for it.
So you take him with you,

41
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:51,166
and when anyone shows up,
I'll tell them that you have him.

42
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:52,751
Someone's gonna be here.
They're gonna come for him.

43
00:04:52,834 --> 00:04:54,044
No, you don't understand.
Really, just, just...

44
00:04:54,085 --> 00:04:57,797
I'm gonna have to put this in here for
like the whole night if nobody comes.

45
00:04:57,881 --> 00:05:01,217
If they're not here, I'll lock him in here
and he'll be safe for the night,

46
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:05,472
but all I can do is take him to the
pound in the morning.

47
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:21,529
Good thing it's Friday,
you know?

48
00:05:21,613 --> 00:05:23,531
We'll find out
where you're headed.

49
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:30,038
Until then, you can stay with me
in a nice warm house.

50
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:32,832
How's that? Yeah?

51
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:43,445
All right.
Here you go.

52
00:06:44,779 --> 00:06:49,409
Sit right here.
Okay, yeah. Here you go.

53
00:06:50,493 --> 00:06:54,706
Okay. Stay, stay.
Chew on those. It's okay.

54
00:06:55,582 --> 00:06:56,666
Stay.

55
00:07:00,628 --> 00:07:01,838
Hello, handsome.

56
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:03,340
Hi.

57
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:05,633
Hi. How'd it go?

58
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:06,718
It was great.

59
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:08,470
Good. You miss me?

60
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:10,055
Not a bit. You?

61
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:12,390
No. Didn't think
about you once.

62
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:17,395
I have a little surprise.

63
00:07:17,479 --> 00:07:21,816
Yeah, well, I have a little
surprise for you, too.

64
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:23,318
Come on. We have
some catching up to do.

65
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:24,527
Yeah.

66
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:29,157
Catching up.
Okay, we'll catch up.

67
00:07:43,797 --> 00:07:45,382
Did you hear something?

68
00:07:45,382 --> 00:07:47,842
That was a branch against the window.

69
00:08:02,816 --> 00:08:08,071
I ran into this interesting
situation at the station tonight.

70
00:08:09,406 --> 00:08:13,618
Why don't you tell me about it in
the morning? How does that sound?

71
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:17,997
What am I gonna do?

72
00:08:37,308 --> 00:08:38,393
Okay, okay.
Okay, it's all right.

73
00:08:38,476 --> 00:08:39,477
Parker!

74
00:08:39,561 --> 00:08:40,895
We had an agreement.
I know, I know.

75
00:08:40,979 --> 00:08:42,147
Or did you forget?

76
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,648
No, I didn't forget.

77
00:08:43,732 --> 00:08:47,944
No, it was... He was at the train station.
I mean, just kind of lost.

78
00:08:48,028 --> 00:08:50,572
Carl was gonna send him to the pound
tomorrow and I thought...

79
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:53,658
You just thought you'd bring him home
and talk me into keeping him, right?

80
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:55,452
No, no, I don't want
to keep him. I don't.

81
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:56,661
Tomorrow morning
I'm getting up,

82
00:08:56,703 --> 00:08:58,329
and I'll find out exactly
where he belongs, okay?

83
00:08:58,371 --> 00:09:00,331
I promise you,
I will do that.

84
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:04,044
All right.
This was Luke's stuff.

85
00:09:04,711 --> 00:09:06,796
Okay, okay.

86
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:10,258
Okay, here you go.
In there.

87
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:13,219
There you go.

88
00:09:13,845 --> 00:09:17,724
Now look. Lots
of good stuff here.

89
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:20,769
That's warm.
You got that.

90
00:09:22,479 --> 00:09:23,563
It's pretty cold.

91
00:09:23,605 --> 00:09:26,483
You like this? Yeah?
This was Luke's favorite.

92
00:09:29,944 --> 00:09:31,946
Okay. Okay,
here's your water.

93
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:38,787
Some story you could tell?
Couldn't you? Yeah.

94
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:41,247
Okay, buddy.

95
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,421
That's better.

96
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:51,633
Good night, buddy.

97
00:10:02,852 --> 00:10:05,939
You know, you're the one
who should be in the doghouse.

98
00:10:06,106 --> 00:10:08,274
I promise I won't bite your toe.

99
00:10:17,659 --> 00:10:19,327
Puppy! Puppy!

100
00:10:19,411 --> 00:10:22,956
Hey, puppy! Come on!
That's good.

101
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:26,793
Good puppy.

102
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,838
Dad, I love him.

103
00:10:30,714 --> 00:10:31,881
Does he have a name yet?

104
00:10:31,965 --> 00:10:34,926
Yes, he does.
"Temporary Guest".

105
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:42,642
You have to keep him.

106
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:46,146
Dad, the house feels so empty
since Luke's been gone.

107
00:10:47,731 --> 00:10:49,399
Ask your mother.

108
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:51,609
Mom?
Yeah?

109
00:10:51,693 --> 00:10:53,695
Could you come
here, please?

110
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:57,574
Look, he even
likes your music.

111
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:58,742
Really!

112
00:10:58,783 --> 00:11:01,327
I can't believe it!
This is a wonder dog!

113
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:03,038
I absolutely have
to keep this dog.

114
00:11:03,121 --> 00:11:04,789
No more dogs.

115
00:11:04,873 --> 00:11:05,832
Don't encourage him.

116
00:11:05,874 --> 00:11:06,875
I won't.

117
00:11:06,958 --> 00:11:08,585
You're so mean.

118
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:12,130
Dad, he's gonna
jump out of that. Here.

119
00:11:12,172 --> 00:11:13,173
Yeah, that's great.

120
00:11:13,256 --> 00:11:14,424
Try this. I love it.

121
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:16,509
Does he fit?
I think so.

122
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:20,263
You in there, bud? Yeah!

123
00:11:20,764 --> 00:11:23,975
No, that's good.
I like it. Great.

124
00:11:24,559 --> 00:11:26,019
So, you saw Michael last night?

125
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:27,187
Yeah.

126
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:30,106
We drove over to the look-out,
watched the comets.

127
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:32,859
It was beautiful.

128
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:34,569
Very romantic.

129
00:11:35,236 --> 00:11:36,821
It was.

130
00:11:37,572 --> 00:11:39,532
Definitely happened more often...

131
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:43,787
Are you the...
Can I help you, pal?

132
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:47,791
Yeah, yeah. I just found this little guy
at the station last night.

133
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:49,334
Can you board him
until we find his owner?

134
00:11:49,376 --> 00:11:50,585
Board him? No,
we can't board him.

135
00:11:50,669 --> 00:11:53,421
This isn't a boarding service.
It's a pound, pal.

136
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:58,218
Look, I just found him.
What am I gonna do with him?

137
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:02,972
Let's see.

138
00:12:03,056 --> 00:12:04,099
Yeah.

139
00:12:04,182 --> 00:12:09,604
He's cute. That'll help with adoption,
but we give them 2 weeks.

140
00:12:10,939 --> 00:12:11,856
Come on.

141
00:12:12,357 --> 00:12:14,150
2 weeks?

142
00:12:14,234 --> 00:12:16,528
Yeah. We're packed.

143
00:12:18,363 --> 00:12:19,989
Excuse me.

144
00:12:23,785 --> 00:12:26,246
I'll call you next week then.
All right. Bye-bye.

145
00:12:26,329 --> 00:12:27,330
Morning, Mary Anne.

146
00:12:27,414 --> 00:12:29,040
How you doing, Parker?

147
00:12:29,541 --> 00:12:32,377
I'm doing great. I was wondering
if I could ask you for a favor.

148
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,295
Sure, anything.

149
00:12:41,636 --> 00:12:44,055
Look at this!

150
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:47,225
Hey, little one!
Hello. Hello!

151
00:12:47,684 --> 00:12:50,270
He's gorgeous!
Where'd you come from?

152
00:12:50,353 --> 00:12:51,980
He was wandering around
the station last night.

153
00:12:52,063 --> 00:12:53,023
Hi, sweetheart.

154
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:54,649
I don't know, it's very strange.

155
00:12:54,733 --> 00:12:57,193
Really?
He's adorable.

156
00:12:57,235 --> 00:12:58,319
I just want to put
that up. Yeah?

157
00:12:58,403 --> 00:12:59,779
Okay, fine, fine.

158
00:12:59,821 --> 00:13:01,489
Window?
Hello. Yeah, right over there.

159
00:13:01,573 --> 00:13:03,241
Any one of those.

160
00:13:03,283 --> 00:13:06,244
Parker, this dog is just fabulous.

161
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:08,455
You wouldn't be interested, would you?

162
00:13:08,538 --> 00:13:10,040
What, the puppy?

163
00:13:10,123 --> 00:13:11,750
A fine young puppy like that.

164
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:14,210
What do you think, Antonia?
New roommate?

165
00:13:15,837 --> 00:13:17,380
No! Antonia!

166
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:21,509
Yeah, yeah.

167
00:13:32,687 --> 00:13:34,022
Morning, Mr. Professor.

168
00:13:34,105 --> 00:13:35,190
Jasjeet.

169
00:13:35,273 --> 00:13:38,651
1 sugar, 2 cream, coming up.
Hey, what have you got there?

170
00:13:38,693 --> 00:13:41,404
I got a new friend here.
You want a dog?

171
00:13:41,488 --> 00:13:43,281
I prefer cash.

172
00:13:43,365 --> 00:13:45,784
He'd be a great guard dog
for you, wouldn't he?

173
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:50,330
Guard dog to guard the hot dogs?
I don't think so.

174
00:13:50,413 --> 00:13:52,540
I don't think so, either.

175
00:13:52,582 --> 00:13:55,669
Seriously, man,
why you want a dog?

176
00:13:55,752 --> 00:13:59,255
Every day you have to walk him,
feed him, clean him, pick up the poop.

177
00:13:59,339 --> 00:14:01,800
How many of these
can I have for him?

178
00:14:01,883 --> 00:14:03,718
On the house.

179
00:14:03,802 --> 00:14:05,553
Too much trouble.
Yeah, you're right.

180
00:14:05,595 --> 00:14:06,596
Thank you, Jas.

181
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:07,972
My pleasure.

182
00:14:09,182 --> 00:14:10,141
Hey, any news?

183
00:14:10,225 --> 00:14:12,686
No. Nobody came, nobody showed up,
nobody called.

184
00:14:12,727 --> 00:14:13,895
Nobody?

185
00:14:15,355 --> 00:14:17,816
Strange. Really strange.

186
00:14:18,858 --> 00:14:20,110
Can you hold him a second?

187
00:14:20,193 --> 00:14:21,236
Yeah.

188
00:14:21,319 --> 00:14:22,904
You're cute.

189
00:14:23,446 --> 00:14:26,324
I made up some flyers.
Would you put that up for me?

190
00:14:26,366 --> 00:14:27,409
Come on.

191
00:14:27,492 --> 00:14:29,911
All right, I'll put them up for you.

192
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:31,329
What a sweetheart you are.

193
00:14:31,413 --> 00:14:32,789
I know, I know, I know.

194
00:14:32,914 --> 00:14:33,957
Come on.

195
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,418
He really likes being in the bag.

196
00:14:36,501 --> 00:14:37,585
Thanks.

197
00:14:37,669 --> 00:14:39,671
Professor, no dogs on the train.

198
00:14:39,754 --> 00:14:40,922
No dogs on the train.

199
00:14:41,006 --> 00:14:42,382
Thank you.

200
00:15:45,487 --> 00:15:47,405
Okay, hold on a second.
Let me try something.

201
00:15:47,447 --> 00:15:49,824
We skip the repeat
of the first section

202
00:15:49,908 --> 00:15:51,701
and go directly
to the lyrical section.

203
00:15:51,785 --> 00:15:53,036
Okay. Let's try that.

204
00:15:53,119 --> 00:15:55,872
But just it means you've got to
build up quicker. You don't have to...

205
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:57,415
And when we get
to the lyrical section,

206
00:15:57,499 --> 00:16:00,377
just big breaths, big breaths.

207
00:16:11,346 --> 00:16:13,306
Don't forget to breathe.

208
00:16:33,410 --> 00:16:34,619
Hello.

209
00:16:44,754 --> 00:16:46,172
That's great.

210
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:52,721
You don't want a puppy,
do you? You want a puppy?

211
00:17:00,395 --> 00:17:02,147
This was the only thing
left on the crate.

212
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:04,024
"Yamanashi".

213
00:17:04,065 --> 00:17:05,358
That's all I can read.

214
00:17:05,442 --> 00:17:06,443
What's that?

215
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:08,945
It's a part of central Japan.

216
00:17:10,864 --> 00:17:12,073
No ordinary dog, Parker.

217
00:17:12,157 --> 00:17:13,158
No.

218
00:17:13,241 --> 00:17:16,411
It's an Akita, or Akita,
as you'd say.

219
00:17:17,162 --> 00:17:18,455
It's a very special breed.

220
00:17:18,538 --> 00:17:19,539
Yeah?

221
00:17:23,335 --> 00:17:25,128
What is that? Hachi.

222
00:17:25,211 --> 00:17:27,088
What?
It's Japanese for "8".

223
00:17:27,130 --> 00:17:28,631
Number of good fortune.

224
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:31,176
Good fortune.

225
00:17:31,217 --> 00:17:32,886
Very nice.

226
00:17:32,927 --> 00:17:35,055
Hachi. Hachi.

227
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:36,723
That's a good name.
I like that.

228
00:17:36,806 --> 00:17:39,309
He might have been born 8th
in the litter.

229
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:41,019
Spiritual significance
in number 8

230
00:17:41,061 --> 00:17:43,605
reaches up to heaven,
comes down to Earth.

231
00:17:46,191 --> 00:17:48,318
So what do you think?
Do you want him?

232
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:49,569
Me?

233
00:17:49,736 --> 00:17:52,572
No, I think he's made his choice.

234
00:17:52,655 --> 00:17:53,823
Meaning what?

235
00:17:54,324 --> 00:17:57,619
Well, meaning he's your problem,
not mine, brother.

236
00:17:58,703 --> 00:18:00,330
You're not a problem,
are you?

237
00:18:00,372 --> 00:18:01,664
Well...

238
00:18:03,041 --> 00:18:08,088
Whether you found him or
he found you, who's to say?

239
00:18:09,214 --> 00:18:10,924
It's meant to be.

240
00:18:10,965 --> 00:18:16,137
He was also saying that the shoguns bred
these Akitas for combat and hunting.

241
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:20,308
So I guess in a way,
they're kind of dog royalty.

242
00:18:21,935 --> 00:18:25,730
Did Ken give you any ideas where
you could find this royal dog a home?

243
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:29,776
I put up 10 flyers already.

244
00:18:31,111 --> 00:18:33,571
You know, someone's
going to claim Hachi.

245
00:18:34,197 --> 00:18:35,782
Who's Hachi?

246
00:18:35,865 --> 00:18:37,075
This...

247
00:18:38,535 --> 00:18:40,954
It's what was on his collar.
That's the symbol.

248
00:18:40,995 --> 00:18:42,455
You named him?
No, I didn't...

249
00:18:42,539 --> 00:18:43,540
Parker, you want to keep him.

250
00:18:43,623 --> 00:18:44,958
No, I do not.
You do. You do.

251
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,501
I don't want to keep him.

252
00:18:46,543 --> 00:18:48,128
Admit it. Admit it. You do.

253
00:18:48,211 --> 00:18:49,754
You want to keep him.
I wasn't even thinking about it.

254
00:18:49,838 --> 00:18:50,797
Yes.

255
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:53,341
Hachi?

256
00:18:56,011 --> 00:18:57,512
Where'd you go?

257
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:03,977
No!

