Good boy.
Stay, go home. Go on.

720
00:53:31,586 --> 00:53:32,712
Go on.

721
00:54:28,727 --> 00:54:30,770
Was it any better that time?

722
00:54:34,649 --> 00:54:35,859
All right.

723
00:54:36,234 --> 00:54:40,488
You remember we were talking about
John Philip Sousa,

724
00:54:40,530 --> 00:54:43,908
great march composer around
the turn of the century?

725
00:54:44,576 --> 00:54:47,662
He was a very famous man,

726
00:54:47,746 --> 00:54:50,832
but he had a huge thing
about recorded music.

727
00:54:50,915 --> 00:54:53,626
He would never allow his music
to be recorded.

728
00:54:53,710 --> 00:54:55,879
Even when Thomas Edison
came to him

729
00:54:55,962 --> 00:54:58,465
with his brand-new
invention, the phonograph.

730
00:54:59,466 --> 00:55:01,718
But Edison didn't care.
He went ahead and did it anyhow.

731
00:55:01,801 --> 00:55:05,930
Secretly he recorded
his marching band in a parade.

732
00:55:07,015 --> 00:55:09,851
Which I guess makes it
the very first bootleg.

733
00:55:13,772 --> 00:55:15,106
So what do you
think about that?

734
00:55:15,148 --> 00:55:17,442
Do you think Sousa was right?

735
00:55:17,525 --> 00:55:19,486
Do you think it's okay now?
What about today's performers?

736
00:55:19,569 --> 00:55:21,571
Should you be able to just walk up
in the middle of a stage,

737
00:55:21,654 --> 00:55:26,368
plug in your CD player to a
Marshall stack and that's it?

738
00:55:26,409 --> 00:55:27,494
It's good enough?

739
00:55:28,912 --> 00:55:30,330
I don't know.

740
00:55:31,956 --> 00:55:35,418
I'm a lot older than you,
but I tend to think that

741
00:55:36,544 --> 00:55:40,674
there's an element of music
that cannot be captured.

742
00:55:40,757 --> 00:55:43,635
Life cannot be captured.
The human heart cannot be captured.

743
00:55:43,677 --> 00:55:46,638
The moment of creation
itself is fleeting.

744
00:56:36,146 --> 00:56:37,981
Hey, Hachi,
how you doing?

745
00:56:39,065 --> 00:56:40,233
Hey, Hachi.

746
00:57:27,530 --> 00:57:28,907
Good night, Hachi.

747
00:57:44,798 --> 00:57:46,174
Hey, buddy.

748
00:57:47,676 --> 00:57:49,260
You ready to go home?

749
00:57:51,554 --> 00:57:52,722
Yeah?

750
00:58:08,279 --> 00:58:11,282
It's all right. It's all right.

751
00:58:27,716 --> 00:58:29,217
Hey, Hachi.

752
00:58:30,885 --> 00:58:32,262
Hey, boy.

753
00:58:43,606 --> 00:58:45,191
Is this how he did it?

754
00:58:46,276 --> 00:58:47,944
I'm sorry. I'll learn.

755
00:58:57,787 --> 00:58:59,080
Andy?

756
00:59:00,540 --> 00:59:02,375
It's time to go, sweetheart.

757
00:59:03,251 --> 00:59:06,254
You're a good boy. You stay here,
okay? I'll be back.

758
00:59:48,546 --> 00:59:52,300
"I hear and behold
God in every object

759
00:59:52,384 --> 00:59:55,303
"Yet understand
God not in the least

760
00:59:55,428 --> 00:59:59,516
"Nor do I understand who there
can be more wonderful than myself

761
00:59:59,599 --> 01:00:03,186
"In the faces of men
and women I see God

762
01:00:03,228 --> 01:00:05,605
"And in my own face
in the glass

763
01:00:05,689 --> 01:00:08,483
"I find letters from God
dropt in the street

764
01:00:08,566 --> 01:00:11,653
"And every one
is sign'd by God's name

765
01:00:11,695 --> 01:00:13,738
"And I leave them
where they are

766
01:00:13,822 --> 01:00:16,741
"For I know that
wherever I go

767
01:00:16,783 --> 01:00:22,080
"Others will punctually
come forever and ever"

768
01:01:18,136 --> 01:01:21,473
Look, you don't have
to wait anymore.

769
01:01:24,309 --> 01:01:26,102
He's not coming back.

770
01:01:37,155 --> 01:01:38,740
All right, Hachi.

771
01:01:40,700 --> 01:01:42,535
You do what you have to do.

772
01:02:27,997 --> 01:02:30,500
Come on, buddy,
come on. Let's go.

773
01:02:30,583 --> 01:02:32,419
Come on, boy. Come on.

774
01:02:35,547 --> 01:02:37,298
Come on, Hachi.

775
01:02:37,382 --> 01:02:38,717
Come on, Hachi.

776
01:02:38,842 --> 01:02:42,262
You're gonna be with us now.
Let's go. Come on.

777
01:02:42,345 --> 01:02:44,097
All right, we gotta go.
Ronnie's waiting.

778
01:02:44,139 --> 01:02:45,348
Come on.

779
01:02:48,059 --> 01:02:50,103
Let me get that for you, sweetie.

780
01:02:54,983 --> 01:02:57,444
Come on, Hach. Up, up, up.
There we go.

781
01:02:57,527 --> 01:02:59,738
That's a good boy. Good.

782
01:03:00,071 --> 01:03:01,531
Good boy, Hachi.

783
01:03:05,285 --> 01:03:07,287
Watch your head...

784
01:03:07,328 --> 01:03:08,955
Good boy.

785
01:04:02,967 --> 01:04:04,469
Hey, there's my guy. Andy?

786
01:04:04,511 --> 01:04:05,595
Yeah?

787
01:04:05,637 --> 01:04:08,306
Hachi! Hachi! Andy!

788
01:04:10,100 --> 01:04:11,059
Hachi!

789
01:04:12,102 --> 01:04:14,896
Hachi, get back here!
Hachi!

790
01:04:16,815 --> 01:04:18,441
Hachi, come on!

791
01:04:21,319 --> 01:04:22,320
Hachi!

792
01:04:24,823 --> 01:04:26,157
Hachi!

793
01:04:30,704 --> 01:04:31,663
Hachi!

794
01:06:43,378 --> 01:06:46,256
Hey, looks like you
got your first visitor.

795
01:06:46,297 --> 01:06:47,799
Hey there, buddy.

796
01:06:48,216 --> 01:06:50,385
Come to welcome us
to our new home?

797
01:07:04,024 --> 01:07:05,150
Hey, Hach.

798
01:07:07,819 --> 01:07:09,696
Hey, Hachi!

799
01:07:09,738 --> 01:07:11,740
What are you doing here?

800
01:07:11,823 --> 01:07:13,450
Lookie, lookie.

801
01:07:18,329 --> 01:07:20,123
He's going right to his spot.

802
01:07:20,165 --> 01:07:21,207
I thought he moved away.

803
01:07:21,291 --> 01:07:22,917
He did.

804
01:07:23,001 --> 01:07:24,753
He looks hungry, yeah?

805
01:07:26,004 --> 01:07:28,298
You are a softie, Jas.

806
01:07:30,425 --> 01:07:32,594
Hey, Hachi.

807
01:07:32,635 --> 01:07:37,098
Want a hot dog, boy?
Go on, boy, have a hot dog.

808
01:07:37,182 --> 01:07:38,767
Hey, Hachi.

809
01:07:39,684 --> 01:07:41,019
Maybe it's your cooking, Jas.

810
01:07:41,102 --> 01:07:42,145
The Jasjeet special.

811
01:07:42,228 --> 01:07:45,482
Come on, you'll like it.
Eat it. It's good for you.

812
01:07:48,610 --> 01:07:50,070
Come on.

813
01:07:50,445 --> 01:07:51,571
It's good.

814
01:07:52,322 --> 01:07:53,990
Where did he come from?

815
01:07:54,074 --> 01:07:55,909
Just showed up.

816
01:07:55,992 --> 01:07:57,702
Come on, boy.
Take it.

817
01:07:58,536 --> 01:08:02,415
You better be careful, Hachi. He's got
hot dogs in there older than you.

818
01:08:03,208 --> 01:08:04,876
Don't listen to them...

819
01:08:20,016 --> 01:08:22,060
Hachi!
God.

820
01:08:22,143 --> 01:08:25,271
Hi! God,
I was so worried about you.

821
01:08:29,317 --> 01:08:31,945
Why is she just
hanging around him?

822
01:08:32,028 --> 01:08:33,947
It's the professor's daughter.
Really?

823
01:08:33,988 --> 01:08:35,990
That's where he's been living.

824
01:08:40,370 --> 01:08:42,163
Will you come home with me?

825
01:08:43,289 --> 01:08:44,249
Hey, hey, hey...

826
01:08:44,332 --> 01:08:45,875
It's all right.
It's okay.

827
01:08:47,293 --> 01:08:48,545
Come on.

828
01:08:48,628 --> 01:08:49,879
Let's go, buddy.

829
01:08:49,921 --> 01:08:51,840
Thank you very much.
Okay.

830
01:08:51,881 --> 01:08:53,341
Thank you!

831
01:08:58,847 --> 01:09:00,432
That's the best thing.

832
01:09:01,516 --> 01:09:03,268
Come on, give me a coffee.

833
01:09:04,644 --> 01:09:06,646
Jasjeet, come on.
Give me a coffee.

834
01:09:20,702 --> 01:09:24,456
I think of him,
too. Every day.

835
01:09:52,734 --> 01:09:53,985
Hey.

836
01:09:55,445 --> 01:09:57,364
You know we love you, Hachi.

837
01:09:58,281 --> 01:10:00,492
We want you
to stay here with us.

838
01:10:04,079 --> 01:10:08,750
But if you have to go,
that's okay, too.

839
01:10:10,627 --> 01:10:11,795
Okay.

840
01:10:31,022 --> 01:10:32,440
Goodbye, Hachi.

841
01:10:44,994 --> 01:10:46,871
Good afternoon, Hachi.

842
01:11:17,068 --> 01:11:18,862
Hey, Hachi.

843
01:11:19,779 --> 01:11:22,782
Here you go.
Don't tell Myra, all right?

844
01:11:25,368 --> 01:11:27,287
Good night, Hachi.

845
01:11:53,730 --> 01:11:55,231
Hello, how are you?

846
01:11:55,273 --> 01:11:56,608
I think...

847
01:12:13,083 --> 01:12:15,627
Lucky! Let's go.

848
01:12:15,710 --> 01:12:17,587
Come on, sweetie.
Hey, Lucky.

849
01:12:19,422 --> 01:12:21,549
Hey, girl. Come on,
Lucky, let's go.

850
01:12:28,556 --> 01:12:30,433
Hey, excuse me, sir.

851
01:12:30,892 --> 01:12:32,435
The dog out there.

852
01:12:32,519 --> 01:12:33,561
Yeah?

853
01:12:33,645 --> 01:12:36,773
Is that the dog that I've been
hearing so much about?

854
01:12:39,359 --> 01:12:41,236
What's it to you?

855
01:12:41,319 --> 01:12:45,657
I'm sorry. I'm Teddy Barnes.
I'm with the Woonsocket Call.

856
01:12:47,742 --> 01:12:49,994
Yeah, I've been hearing a lot
of talk about him on the trains.

857
01:12:50,078 --> 01:12:53,081
I don't know, sounds like
it could make a good story.

858
01:12:56,126 --> 01:12:58,878
It's Boilins,
Carl Boilins.

859
01:12:58,962 --> 01:13:03,341
B-O-I-L-I-N-S. Yes.
There's no "Y" in there.

860
01:13:03,425 --> 01:13:05,885
I'm the one that found him,
handed him over.

861
01:13:06,136 --> 01:13:07,387
Yeah?

862
01:13:07,429 --> 01:13:11,891
So, Carl, where's he live?

863
01:13:11,975 --> 01:13:16,396
Well, we're not really sure.
He comes and goes.

864
01:13:17,272 --> 01:13:18,398
Nobody bothers him?

865
01:13:18,481 --> 01:13:20,692
No, we put up with him.

866
01:13:20,775 --> 01:13:23,028
He just does what he's doing.

867
01:13:23,069 --> 01:13:25,697
Hey, you mind if I take a picture?

868
01:13:26,531 --> 01:13:27,532
For the newspaper.

869
01:13:27,615 --> 01:13:29,325
I don't mind if Hachi don't mind.

870
01:13:29,409 --> 01:13:32,829
Thank you very much.
Very nice, very nice.

871
01:13:32,871 --> 01:13:34,956
One without first, please.

872
01:13:35,081 --> 01:13:37,500
Without the dog?
All right. Stay there.

873
01:13:38,710 --> 01:13:40,295
Well, I...

874
01:13:41,379 --> 01:13:42,756
Yeah. All right.

875
01:13:42,839 --> 01:13:44,049
I appreciate it.

876
01:13:44,132 --> 01:13:45,467
That's very kind of you.

877
01:13:47,969 --> 01:13:49,220
Okay, nice and tight.
Yeah.

878
01:13:49,304 --> 01:13:50,930
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

879
01:13:51,014 --> 01:13:51,931
Look at that there.

880
01:13:52,015 --> 01:13:53,266
Big smile.

881
01:13:54,184 --> 01:13:58,021
That's... That's beautiful.
Thank you.

882
01:14:12,285 --> 01:14:13,787
Hey, Hachi.

883
01:14:15,580 --> 01:14:19,376
This kid in Derry
sent you his lunch money.

884
01:14:20,168 --> 01:14:22,462
He wants me to buy
you treats with it.

885
01:14:23,546 --> 01:14:25,465
It's like the 3rd one this week.

886
01:14:25,548 --> 01:14:29,386
If this keeps up, I'll have to open
a bank account for you.

887
01:14:30,387 --> 01:14:32,430
Don't say I never
gave you nothing.

888
01:14:35,183 --> 01:14:37,560
The dog's making out
like a bandit here.

889
01:14:37,936 --> 01:14:39,979
Look at this, isn't that cute?

890
01:14:41,981 --> 01:14:43,149
Hey, Hach.

891
01:14:43,733 --> 01:14:44,734
What are you doing with the money?

892
01:14:44,818 --> 01:14:45,860
I'm his executor.

893
01:14:56,329 --> 01:14:58,123
Be right with you, sir.

894
01:14:59,499 --> 01:15:03,837
{y:i}River Junction local is now boarding
{y:i}on track 2, it's making all stops.

895
01:15:13,722 --> 01:15:15,140
Hachi.

896
01:15:20,061 --> 01:15:21,938
Here you go, Hachi.

897
01:15:22,689 --> 01:15:24,065
There you are.

898
01:15:24,774 --> 01:15:25,859
Hungry?

899
01:15:26,484 --> 01:15:29,571
Yes, he's very cold.
He must eat.

900
01:15:31,698 --> 01:15:34,367
I'm Jasjeet.
I run the hot dog stand.

901
01:15:34,576 --> 01:15:37,203
I'm Ken Fujiyoshi,
Professor Wilson's friend.

902
01:15:37,287 --> 01:15:38,997
Mr. Professor?

903
01:15:40,248 --> 01:15:41,708
1 sugar, 2 cream.

904
01:15:43,460 --> 01:15:45,295
So then you must have read
the article, then?

905
01:15:45,378 --> 01:15:46,379
I did.

906
01:15:46,421 --> 01:15:47,797
You saw my name in the article?

907
01:15:49,090 --> 01:15:50,550
Yes, I did.

908
01:15:50,592 --> 01:15:51,801
Twice.

909
01:15:51,885 --> 01:15:53,887
Please, let me help
with the expense.

910
01:15:53,970 --> 01:15:55,930
No, no, please. No money.

911
01:15:56,014 --> 01:15:58,099
What if he gets sick?
Medical expenses?

912
01:15:58,183 --> 01:16:00,018
We'll take a collection.

913
01:16:00,101 --> 01:16:04,731
From the travelers, the vendors,
and we will take care of it for him.

914
01:16:04,856 --> 01:16:06,858
The station square
is Hachi's home now.

915
01:16:06,900 --> 01:16:10,278
Every day he comes, same time,
same place, here only.

916
01:16:10,362 --> 01:16:11,571
You'll do that for him?

917
01:16:11,654 --> 01:16:14,908
Take care of him?
Of course.

918
01:16:17,202 --> 01:16:18,661
All right, then I...

919
01:16:19,496 --> 01:16:22,332
I've got to sell some hot dogs.
Good to meet you.

920
01:16:22,374 --> 01:16:24,918
You, too.
Thank you very much.

921
01:16:29,089 --> 01:16:30,382
It's been a year, hasn't it?

922
01:16:33,343 --> 01:16:35,762
I wake up sometimes
in the middle of the night

923
01:16:36,054 --> 01:16:38,807
and think about Parker.
He was a good friend.

924
01:16:39,683 --> 01:16:42,602
I understand how you feel.

925
01:16:43,728 --> 01:16:46,856
Hachi, my friend,
Parker is never coming home.

926
01:16:47,273 --> 01:16:50,485
But if Hachiko wants to wait,
then Hachiko should wait.

927
01:16:50,694 --> 01:16:54,072
You want to wait for him,
don't you?

928
01:16:57,033 --> 01:17:00,995
Have a long life Hachi.

929
01:17:12,048 --> 01:17:17,512
Come on, mister. There we are.
That's a good boy.

930
01:17:21,641 --> 01:17:24,769
Want some more?
Okay, come on.

931
01:17:27,814 --> 01:17:32,360
Okay, come on, boy.
Last piece. It's good?

932
01:17:45,540 --> 01:17:47,334
See you tomorrow, Hachi.

933
01:17:49,085 --> 01:17:50,337
Ciao, Hachi.

934
01:18:26,623 --> 01:18:28,750
{y:i}Final call for Oakland,

935
01:18:28,792 --> 01:18:31,961
{y:i}Wood River Junction
{y:i}and 4 Corners

936
01:18:32,045 --> 01:18:33,672
{y:i}leaving from track 2.

937
01:18:51,731 --> 01:18:54,109
Ms. Wilson?
Nice to see you again.

938
01:18:54,150 --> 01:18:55,985
Good afternoon.
Thank you.

939
01:18:57,487 --> 01:18:59,531
That's the professor's wife?

940
01:20:00,050 --> 01:20:01,217
Cate.

941
01:20:05,305 --> 01:20:06,431
Ken.

942
01:20:09,517 --> 01:20:11,144
It's been a while.

943
01:20:12,020 --> 01:20:13,772
It certainly has.

944
01:20:24,199 --> 01:20:27,952
It's 10 years.
Can you believe it?

945
01:20:43,551 --> 01:20:44,844
Hi, Hachi.

946
01:20:51,518 --> 01:20:52,936
Hi, Hachi.

947
01:21:11,830 --> 01:21:13,581
All right, have a good one.

948
01:21:13,665 --> 01:21:14,666
Thank you, Jas.

949
01:21:22,382 --> 01:21:23,925
Who would've thought?
I know.

950
01:21:24,009 --> 01:21:26,428
I mean, when we first
went in there, I was like...

951
01:21:38,023 --> 01:21:39,274
Hachi?

952
01:21:46,322 --> 01:21:47,949
Hachi?

953
01:21:51,911 --> 01:21:54,831
You old thing, you're still waiting.

954
01:22:10,263 --> 01:22:11,806
That's right.

955
01:22:27,989 --> 01:22:31,493
If it's all right, could I wait with you
for the next train?

956
01:22:34,621 --> 01:22:35,914
Yeah?

957
01:22:37,791 --> 01:22:39,167
Thanks.

958
01:22:49,010 --> 01:22:50,303
Hachi.

959
01:23:03,692 --> 01:23:04,901
That's so cute.
You like that one?

960
01:23:04,984 --> 01:23:06,403
Yeah.
Yeah.

961
01:23:06,444 --> 01:23:07,946
That's good, isn't it?

962
01:23:08,029 --> 01:23:09,072
That's me.

963
01:23:09,155 --> 01:23:11,157
I know, I remember.

964
01:23:11,700 --> 01:23:15,245
I remember. I was there that day.
I took that picture.

965
01:23:16,162 --> 01:23:17,956
He still looks so cute.

966
01:23:20,458 --> 01:23:21,584
He went to the wedding.

967
01:23:21,668 --> 01:23:24,546
Yeah. He's right there.

968
01:23:25,547 --> 01:23:26,798
Right there.

969
01:23:26,840 --> 01:23:29,259
Where did Grandpa find Hachi?

970
01:23:30,510 --> 01:23:34,014
Ronnie, actually,
Hachi found your grandfather.

971
01:23:34,097 --> 01:23:35,181
How?

972
01:23:36,808 --> 01:23:41,229
One night your grandfather was
coming back from a trip.

973
01:23:42,439 --> 01:23:44,441
He got off at the train station,

974
01:23:45,692 --> 01:23:47,777
he went inside
of the train station...

975
01:25:43,309 --> 01:25:44,686
Hey, boy.

976
01:25:46,396 --> 01:25:50,316
Hey! Come on, let's go.
Come on!

977
01:26:18,303 --> 01:26:20,013
Hachi!

978
01:26:20,388 --> 01:26:22,098
Hey, boy.

979
01:26:25,060 --> 01:26:30,857
Subtitles: Arigon

980
01:27:04,849 --> 01:27:06,810
I never met my grandfather.

981
01:27:07,686 --> 01:27:09,896
He died when I was just a baby.

982
01:27:09,979 --> 01:27:15,694
But when I hear about him and Hachi,
I feel like I know him.

983
01:27:16,319 --> 01:27:19,364
They taught me
the meaning of loyalty,

984
01:27:19,447 --> 01:27:22,992
that you should never forget
anyone that you've loved.

985
01:27:23,785 --> 01:27:27,205
And that's why Hachi will
forever be my hero.

986
01:27:38,299 --> 01:27:40,051
My God, look how cute he is!
Hi, boy.

987
01:27:40,093 --> 01:27:41,761
He drives me crazy.

988
01:27:41,845 --> 01:27:43,054
He's happy to see somebody.

989
01:27:43,138 --> 01:27:44,222
I know.

990
01:27:46,349 --> 01:27:47,934
Can you walk?

991
01:27:51,563 --> 01:27:53,356
Come on, Hachi.
Let's go.

992
01:27:56,901 --> 01:27:58,319
Come on.

993
01:28:00,447 --> 01:28:02,115
Hey, here boy.
